  "notes": "{左折|させつ} is the formal/technical term for turning left, commonly used in traffic contexts and directions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {左折|させつ}する: to turn left\n- {左折|させつ}{禁止|きんし}: no left turn\n- {左折|させつ}{車線|しゃせん}: left turn lane\n- {左折|させつ}{専用|せんよう}: left turn only\n\nTRAFFIC NOTES:\n- In Japan, driving is on the left, so {左折|させつ} is similar to right turns in countries with right-side driving\n- Watch for {巻|ま}き{込|こ}み (cyclists/pedestrians in blind spot)",
